---Task Retry Policy is implemented on a best-effort basis. The default policy retries tasks with a minimum_backoff of 60 seconds, and a maximum_backoff of 12 hours. You can disable the policy by setting the task_retry_disabled field to true. Retry delay will be exponential based on provided minimum and maximum backoffs. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_backoff. Note that the delay between consecutive task restarts may not always precisely match the configured settings. This can happen when the ConnectCluster is in rebalancing state or if the ConnectCluster is unresponsive etc. The default values for minimum and maximum backoffs are 60 seconds and 12 hours respectively.
---@class gcp.managedkafka_v1.TaskRetryPolicy
---@field maximumBackoff? string Optional. The maximum amount of time to wait before retrying a failed task. This sets an upper bound for the backoff delay.
---@field taskRetryDisabled? boolean Optional. If true, task retry is disabled.
---@field minimumBackoff? string Optional. The minimum amount of time to wait before retrying a failed task. This sets a lower bound for the backoff delay.

---The TLS configuration for the Kafka cluster.
---@class gcp.managedkafka_v1.TlsConfig
---@field trustConfig? gcp.managedkafka_v1.TrustConfig Optional. The configuration of the broker truststore. If specified, clients can use mTLS for authentication.
---@field sslPrincipalMappingRules? string Optional. A list of rules for mapping from SSL principal names to short names. These are applied in order by Kafka. Refer to the Apache Kafka documentation for `ssl.principal.mapping.rules` for the precise formatting details and syntax. Example: "RULE:^CN=(.*?),OU=ServiceUsers.*$/$1@example.com/,DEFAULT" This is a static Kafka broker configuration. Setting or modifying this field will trigger a rolling restart of the Kafka brokers to apply the change. An empty string means no rules are applied (Kafka default).

---A Kafka topic in a given cluster.
---@class gcp.managedkafka_v1.Topic
---@field configs? gcp.managedkafka_v1.StringMap Optional. Configurations for the topic that are overridden from the cluster defaults. The key of the map is a Kafka topic property name, for example: `cleanup.policy`, `compression.type`.
---@field replicationFactor? number Required. Immutable. The number of replicas of each partition. A replication factor of 3 is recommended for high availability.
---@field name? string Identifier. The name of the topic. The `topic` segment is used when connecting directly to the cluster. Structured like: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/clusters/{cluster}/topics/{topic}
---@field partitionCount? number Required. The number of partitions this topic has. The partition count can only be increased, not decreased. Please note that if partitions are increased for a topic that has a key, the partitioning logic or the ordering of the messages will be affected.

---@alias gcp.managedkafka_v1.TopicList gcp.managedkafka_v1.Topic[]

---Sources of CA certificates to install in the broker's truststore.
---@class gcp.managedkafka_v1.TrustConfig
---@field casConfigs? gcp.managedkafka_v1.CertificateAuthorityServiceConfigList Optional. Configuration for the Google Certificate Authority Service. Maximum 10.

---UpdateOptions specifies options that influence how a cluster update is applied. These options control the behavior of the update process, rather than defining the desired end-state of a cluster.
